      ":question/id": "05d3989d-1da3-57a6-ac84-893d2cb998a4",
      ":question/problem": "The circle $x^2+y^2=25$ has a tangent at $(3,4)$ that meets the $y$-axis at $P$.\n\n![Circle with the tangent through (3,4) meeting the y-axis at P.](images/3b/3b7add027c857979a54396568b0c0a6928060f97b1af2e2a6b8520bebb025ec0.png)\n\nImplicit differentiation has been started for you:\n\n$$\n2x+2y\\frac{dy}{dx}=0.\n$$\n\nFind the coordinates of $P$. Use the tangent slope in $y-4=m(x-3)$, and remember that $x=0$ on the $y$-axis.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Solve the given differentiated equation for the tangent slope:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{x}{y}.\n$$\n\nAt $(3,4)$, the tangent slope is $m=-\\frac{3}{4}$. The tangent line is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-4&=-\\frac{3}{4}(x-3) \\\\\ny&=-\\frac{3}{4}x+\\frac{25}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet $x=0$ to find its intersection with the $y$-axis. This gives $y=\\frac{25}{4}$, so\n\n$$\nP=\\left(0,\\frac{25}{4}\\right).\n$$"
    },
