      ":question/id": "0b87b4aa-91d2-54c2-88bf-5d19ba04843f",
      ":question/problem": "The curve has equation $4 x^{2} + 2 y^{2}=18$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(-2,1\\right)$ meets the $y$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nUse $y-y_0=m(x-x_0)$ with the given point. On the $y$-axis, $x=0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8 x+\\left(4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(4 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(8 x\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{8 x}{4 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{-16}{4}=4\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=4$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(1\\right)&=4\\left(x-\\left(-2\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=4\\left(x-\\left(-2\\right)\\right)+\\left(1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=4\\left(0-\\left(-2\\right)\\right)+\\left(1\\right) \\\\\ny&=9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(0,9\\right)$."
    },
