      ":question/id": "46873e73-7f1a-5df2-b6ff-b1662bed6345",
      ":question/problem": "The curve has equation $2 x^{2} + 4 y^{2}=72$. The **tangent** line at $\\left(2,-4\\right)$ meets the $x$-axis at $P$. Find the coordinates of $P$.\n\nUse $y-y_0=m(x-x_0)$ with the given point. On the $x$-axis, $y=0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Treat $y$ as a function of $x$. Differentiate implicitly and collect the derivative terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4 x+\\left(8 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=0 \\\\\n\\left(8 y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\left(4 x\\right) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{4 x}{8 y}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the given point:\n\n$$\nm_{\\mathrm{t}}=-\\frac{8}{-32}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nThe tangent line uses $m=\\frac{1}{4}$.\n\nUse the given point and this slope:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-4\\right)&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right) \\\\\ny&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$. Substitute and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)+\\left(-4\\right) \\\\\nx-\\left(2\\right)&=-\\frac{-4}{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\\nx&=18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore $P=\\left(18,0\\right)$."
    },
